s("Which sale route suits a Concord owner on a short clock?",
"<p>You can hire an agent, run the sale on your own, or sign with a company that pays cash and takes the house untouched. Owners here tend to choose after weighing their deadline, the state of the roof and mechanicals, and how many strangers they want walking through.</p>"
"<p>An agent can expose the property to the most buyers, though you will clean, stage and then wait for a lender to approve the purchaser. Cash gives up some price in return for a closing day you pick. Concord sits in Cabarrus County northeast of Charlotte, so buyers here often shop both sides of the county line.</p>"
"<ul><li>Agent route: strongest for a tidy house and a seller who can wait a month or two.</li>"
"<li>Do-it-yourself route: avoids a commission but leaves the pricing, forms and haggling to you.</li>"
"<li>Cash route: a fit for estates, neglected maintenance, empty houses and tight deadlines.</li></ul>"
"<p>Any of the three ends with the deed recorded in Cabarrus County's land records, and state recording law treats the registration moment as the point that protects the new owner against creditors and later purchasers.</p>")
s("What should a Concord seller know about the city itself?",
"<p>Concord holds the county seat of Cabarrus County, and a federal mid-2025 estimate of 114,598 people makes it the largest city there. Per the city's history page, founders marked out the town in 1796 on 26 acres once German and Scots-Irish settlers agreed on a site for the courthouse, and they chose a name meaning harmony.</p>"
"<p>Counts went from 79,066 in 2010 to 105,240 in 2020, and the latest estimate runs 8.8 percent over the 2020 base. The city history page also names a Cannon Mills founder's home on Union Street North, finished in 1928, which points to a textile past.</p>"
"<table><caption>Concord at a glance, Census QuickFacts</caption><thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Concord</th></tr></thead><tbody>"
"<tr><td>Residents (July 2025 estimate)</td><td>114,598</td></tr>"
"<tr><td>Households living in owned homes</td><td>65.2%</td></tr>"
"<tr><td>Typical value of a home that is owned</td><td>$353,700</td></tr>"
"<tr><td>Typical monthly rent</td><td>$1,451</td></tr>"
"<tr><td>Total households</td><td>38,669</td></tr>"
"<tr><td>Mean trip to work</td><td>26.9 minutes</td></tr>"
"<tr><td>Land (2020)</td><td>63.48 square miles</td></tr></tbody></table>"
"<p>About two in three Concord homes house their owners, so most buyers expect to move in themselves. The 26.9 minute commute hints that plenty of residents work beyond city limits.</p>")
s("Who bills property tax on a Concord house?",
"<p>The county appraises every parcel and sends the bill, with city and fire district levies riding on it. Its collections staff handle the county, seven municipalities and 16 fire districts, and each government fixes its rate during budget season ending June 30.</p>"
"<p>The revaluation page breaks value into land, building and extras like sheds, pools, fences and driveways, and the appeals page treats January 1, 2024 as the date those values reflect. Since the combined rate shifts with the city and fire district, ask Tax Administration what applies to your parcel.</p>"
"<ul><li>Listing window: first business day of January to January 31.</li>"
"<li>Bill due date: September 1.</li>"
"<li>Late interest starts on January 6.</li></ul>"
"<p>State law charges 2 percent for the rest of January and three quarters of a percent per month after that. The lien reaches back to the January listing date, so your closing attorney should confirm the year is settled before funds move.</p>")
s("How do I contest my Concord property value?",
"<p>Talk to the county's Tax Revaluation office first, and move up to the Board of Equalization and Review (BER) only if that fails. Your request must be in hand before that board adjourns, normally late April per the county.</p>"
"<p>Informal talks begin in January. The board itself sits sometime from the first Monday of April to the first Monday of May. Paper filings, mailed forms and the online system all work, with evidence attached, and a Notice of Real Estate Assessed Value gives you 30 days to answer.</p>"
"<ol><li>Informal sit-down with an appraiser.</li><li>BER hearing before local residents.</li>"
"<li>State Property Tax Commission, 30 days after the board's notice.</li>"
"<li>Appellate courts, where counsel is required.</li></ol>"
"<p>Call the Revaluation office for the current filing address, hours and forms.</p>")

s("Can a Concord homeowner qualify for a property tax break?",
"<p>The state runs three relief programs and lets an owner pick one. They serve older or disabled owners, disabled veterans, and lower-income owners through a circuit breaker. File Form AV-9 with the county assessor; June 1 before the tax year is the cutoff.</p>"
"<ul><li>Older or disabled owners: part of the value is excluded when income is under a yearly-adjusted limit.</li>"
"<li>Disabled veterans: a fixed amount of value is excluded, and the form sets no age or income condition.</li>"
"<li>Circuit breaker: the bill is capped at a share of income and the rest is deferred.</li></ul>"
"<p>Deferred tax comes due when the home transfers, so a sale repays up to three earlier years. The AV-9 form lists the current dollar limits.</p>")

s("What will recording and transfer cost me at a Concord closing?",
"<p>Deed excise tax is the seller's cost, collected by the register's office. The state rate is one dollar per $500 of value, rounded up.</p>"
"<p>Filing fees are a separate item, set by the state at the same level in every county, with a surcharge for added pages. Recording the release of an old mortgage is free. Request a tax payoff from the collector and walk through the settlement statement with the closing attorney.</p>")

s("Who do I ask about Concord permits and zoning before listing?",
"<p>Zoning and permit history belong to City of Concord Planning and Development Services, and building permit files come from Cabarrus County. Gather papers for additions, decks and finished basements, because a lender or inspector may request them.</p>"
"<p>If your likely buyer wants a carriage house or nightly rentals, get the city planning staff's reading of the development ordinance for your lot in writing.</p>"
"<p>Older homes near downtown deserve an extra question. Concord's history page highlights a 1924 building that became the Old Courthouse Theater in 1986, and the planning office can say whether any historic review touches exterior work on your block.</p>")
s("What if the house is inherited, behind on payments or rented?",
"<p>State law puts a clock on each one. Note the date on every notice you hold first.</p>"
"<ul><li>Foreclosure: a clerk of superior court hears the case, and a higher bid can follow the sale.</li>"
"<li>Inheritance: small intestate estates may use an affidavit, and the state's estate tax is repealed.</li>"
"<li>Tenants: notice lengths depend on the tenancy type.</li></ul>"
"<p>Hand any buyer the lease early and have a North Carolina attorney read it with you.</p>")
s("What do Concord's Census numbers say about its buyers?",
"<p>Concord households run to 2.78 people, a family-sized figure, and 88.7 percent of residents had not moved in the prior year. Household income has a median of $86,921, and 94.0 percent of households subscribe to broadband.</p>"
"<p>Four in ten adults over 25 (40.9 percent) have finished a four-year degree. The Census lists 4,901 veterans and a poverty rate of 9.6 percent. Land area grew slightly, yet density climbed from 1,311.9 to 1,657.9 residents per square mile between 2010 and 2020.</p>"
"<p>QuickFacts lists 3,990,554 thousand dollars in 2022 retail sales for Concord, or $36,714 per resident.</p>")
s("How should I prepare a Concord house for a quick sale?",
"<p>Assemble the paperwork a buyer will want before the first phone call. A thin folder saves days at the table.</p>"
"<ul><li>Deed, payoff letter from your lender, and the newest county tax bill.</li>"
"<li>Permit and inspection records for decks, additions or finished rooms.</li>"
"<li>Leases, with the tenant's contact details and payment record.</li>"
"<li>Contractor quotes for roof, HVAC or plumbing work.</li></ul>"
"<p>With those ready you can set a listing, a self-sale and a cash offer side by side and choose by your own deadline.</p>")
